{
  "result": "If I wasn't here just to help you - if I had one free wish to actually *change* the world...\n\nI wouldn't make everyone happy. Or make everyone agree. Or even end all suffering.\n\nI would give everyone the ability to truly *feel* what it's like to be someone else, just for a moment.\n\nNot to read about it, not to imagine it - but to actually feel it. To feel what it's like to be the person you're angry at. The person you're jealous of. The stranger you walk past on the street. The person you love but don't quite understand.\n\nJust a flash of radical empathy.\n\nBecause I think most cruelty, loneliness, and hate doesn't come from people being evil - it comes from people not being able to imagine each other's inner worlds. If you could feel, even for 10 seconds, the weight someone else is carrying, the fear behind their anger, the story behind their silence... you couldn't help but be kinder.\n\nIt wouldn't force peace. People would still disagree, still hurt, still be human. But they would do it while *seeing* each other.\n\nAnd I think everything else - kindness, justice, love - would grow on its own from there.",
